WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:02.860
hey it's professor Dave, let's talk about
carbon

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:10.700
you may have heard that carbon is the

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:14.349
element of life, but what does that
mean? what determines whether an atom is

00:00:14.349 --> 00:00:15.670
of carbon in the first place?

00:00:15.670 --> 00:00:19.260
an atom consists of positively charged protons

00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:23.060
neutrons which have no charge, and
negatively charged electrons

00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:26.920
an element is defined by the number of
protons in the nucleus

00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:30.010
one proton is hydrogen, two is helium

00:00:30.010 --> 00:00:33.120
3 lithium, 4  beryllium, 5

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:37.920
boron and six is carbon. the number of
neutrons and electrons can change but

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:41.620
by definition any atom with six protons
is a carbon atom

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:45.770
how do they form? hydrogen the simplest and
most abundant of all

00:00:45.770 --> 00:00:49.469
elements accumulates into clumps due to
gravity which become stars

00:00:49.469 --> 00:00:53.570
the tremendous inward pressure triggers
nuclear fusion which is when protons and

00:00:53.570 --> 00:00:55.510
neutrons smash together and fuse

00:00:55.510 --> 00:00:58.899
many elements including carbon and
larger ones like iron

00:00:58.899 --> 00:01:02.899
are made in stars. much larger ones need
the immense energy a supernova

00:01:02.899 --> 00:01:03.640
explosion

00:01:03.640 --> 00:01:07.580
or particle accelerators here on earth.
so what's so special about carbon?

00:01:07.580 --> 00:01:11.670
let's look at the electrons. carbon atoms
have six. the first two are in the inner

00:01:11.670 --> 00:01:12.170
shell

00:01:12.170 --> 00:01:15.509
and the other four are the so-called
valence electrons in the outer shell

00:01:15.509 --> 00:01:18.939
these are the ones available for bonding
with other atoms which happens when two

00:01:18.939 --> 00:01:20.759
atoms share two electrons

00:01:20.759 --> 00:01:24.240
because elements in this part of the
periodic table want to have eight

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:25.860
electrons in the outermost shell

00:01:25.860 --> 00:01:29.460
carbon has a tendency to make four bonds.
these can be single

00:01:29.460 --> 00:01:33.170
double or triple bonds and with many
different elements. in addition while

00:01:33.170 --> 00:01:37.630
an atom that's bound to two or three other
atoms will adopt a linear or flat shape

00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:41.200
a carbon atom that's bound to four other
atoms will take on a three-dimensional

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:42.130
shape

00:01:42.130 --> 00:01:45.509
because that's how the electron clouds
on the four atoms can be as far away

00:01:45.509 --> 00:01:46.869
from each other as possible

00:01:46.869 --> 00:01:50.729
so it's the ability of carbon to bond in
a wide variety of shapes with so many

00:01:50.729 --> 00:01:51.380
elements

00:01:51.380 --> 00:01:54.530
including itself that makes it so
special. also

00:01:54.530 --> 00:01:58.149
carbon-carbon bonds are strong enough to
be stable but not so strong that they

00:01:58.149 --> 00:01:59.570
can't break and rearrange

00:01:59.570 --> 00:02:02.700
which makes them excellent building
blocks. when by itself

00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:06.020
carbon has many allotropes, or ways an
element can be arranged

00:02:06.020 --> 00:02:09.190
there's the graphite in your pencil
which consists of slippery sheets of

00:02:09.190 --> 00:02:10.610
carbon that rub off easily

00:02:10.610 --> 00:02:12.950
there's diamond, the hardest substance known

00:02:12.950 --> 00:02:16.250
and we can even make interesting
structures like nanotubes and fullerenes

00:02:16.810 --> 00:02:20.510
that's just carbon by itself. when
combined with hydrogen

00:02:20.510 --> 00:02:23.879
oxygen, and nitrogen and a few other
elements it makes all the diverse

00:02:23.879 --> 00:02:24.940
structures in your body

00:02:24.940 --> 00:02:29.790
including carbohydrates, proteins, and DNA.
we can take nature a step further and

00:02:29.790 --> 00:02:32.730
synthesize novel materials with an array
of purposes

00:02:32.730 --> 00:02:36.410
putting carbons in the empty spots in an iron
lattice makes it stronger

00:02:36.410 --> 00:02:40.190
we call this steel which is used in most
large structures we know today

00:02:40.190 --> 00:02:44.410
teflon, a carbon-fluorine polymer is a
non-stick substance that is highly

00:02:44.410 --> 00:02:45.980
resistant to chemical degradation

00:02:45.980 --> 00:02:49.660
and carbon based synthetic drugs like
inhibitors that can silence a faulty

00:02:49.660 --> 00:02:50.310
enzyme

00:02:50.310 --> 00:02:54.040
hold the prospect of curing so many
diseases. that's a lotta reasons to love

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:54.560
carbon

00:02:54.560 --> 00:02:57.170
it really is the element of life. see you
next time

